column9:
I would argue that Javascript has a standard way to build an object hierarchy.  It's just that people find it bitter and can't help but add some syntactic sugar.<p>bitter:<p>myClass.prototype = new parentClass;<p>myClass.constructor = function(){...}<p>---------------------------<p>sweet (relatively speaking):<p>myClass = Class({<p><pre><code>    Extends: parentClass,

    initialize: function(){...}
</code></pre>
})
